---
interface Props { compact?: boolean }
const { compact = false } = Astro.props;
---
{compact ? (
  <p class="yardley-entry-compact">Still working out the details? <a class="card-link" href="/job/">Meet Yardley, your AI mixer guide →</a></p>
) : (
  <aside class="yardley-entry" aria-label="Meet Yardley, the AI mixer guide">
    <div class="wrap yardley-entry-inner">
      <div class="yardley-entry-lead">
        <span class="yardley-mark" aria-hidden="true">Y<span>/</span></span>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">AI mixer guide</p>
          <h2>Yardley works out which mixer fits.</h2>
          <p class="lede">Yardley is the AI guide for this lineup. Tell it the work, the pour, and whether a chassis is already in hand. It asks what is still missing, then names one or two StarMix units from published specs. You review the brief. Paul confirms the machine.</p>
          <a class="btn" href="/job/">Work out my fit</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps yardley-entry-steps">
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step-n">01</span>
          <h3>Tell it the job</h3>
          <p>A sentence is enough. The choices are there when you would rather tap than type.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step-n">02</span>
          <h3>Get a shortlist</h3>
          <p>One primary unit and, at most, one alternate. Figures come from the published lineup.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step-n">03</span>
          <h3>Review, then send</h3>
          <p>Nothing goes to Paul until you submit. He confirms the machine and the configuration.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </aside>
)}
